		<ThingDef ParentName="SweetMealBase">
		<defName>IceCreamfruits</defName>
		<label>IceCream(fruits)</label>
		<description>Finally, the crowning glory of RimWorld's culinary madness is this ice cream - a crispy cone of ground-up Mekhanite filled with a "cream" made from hydroponic milk (which may have been a poisonous mushroom in a past life), generously topped with fruit picked by... well, you know who.</description>
		<graphicData>
			<texPath>Things/Item/Meal/Icecream/IceCreamfruits</texPath>
			<graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
		</graphicData>
		<statBases>
			<DeteriorationRate>10</DeteriorationRate>
			<MarketValue>14</MarketValue>
			<Bulk>1.0</Bulk>
			<Mass>0.7</Mass>
			<Nutrition>0.1</Nutrition>
		</statBases>
		<ingestible>
			<nurseable>true</nurseable>
			<maxNumToIngestAtOnce>1</maxNumToIngestAtOnce>
			<preferability>DesperateOnly</preferability>
			<joy>0.5</joy>
			<ingestEffect>EatVegetarian</ingestEffect>
			<ingestSound>Meal_Eat</ingestSound>
			<joyKind>Gluttonous</joyKind>
			<outcomeDoers>
				<li Class="IngestionOutcomeDoer_GiveHediff">
					<hediffDef>HadIceCream</hediffDef>
					<severity>0.1</severity>
				</li>
			</outcomeDoers>
		</ingestible>
		<comps>
			<li Class="CompProperties_Drug">
				<addictiveness>0</addictiveness>
				<listOrder>1300</listOrder>
			</li>
			<li Class="CompProperties_Rottable">

				<daysToRotStart>1</daysToRotStart>
				<rotDestroys>true</rotDestroys>
			</li>
		</comps>
	</ThingDef>
	
		<ThingDef ParentName="SweetMealBase">
		<defName>IceCreamchocolate</defName>
		<label>IceCream(chocolate)</label>
		<description>"The Imperial scientists debated for a long time whether this sticky mass could be considered real food. In the end, the Main Food Algorithm ruled that if a colonist eats it voluntarily, it is edible. Although the case of Private Johnson dying of joy after the first spoonful is still under investigation.
*It is extracted from cocoa beans grown on southern plantations where only happy (and completely voluntary) workers work. At least, that's what the reports for the Imperial Inspectorate say. The chocolate itself goes through 17 stages of purification, after which only 3% sand, 1% insects and 0.5% memories of freedom remain in it."*.</description>
